    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a **soft-delete**: the record is retained and flagged, and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks skip flagged owners.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `deleted` boolean field (column `deleted`, non-null, default `false`) with `isDeleted()` / `setDeleted(...)`. A newly created owner defaults to `false`.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 `deleteOwner(...)` now marks the owner deleted and persists it via `ownerRepository.save(...)` instead of removing the row. The endpoint keeps returning `204 No Content` (2xx), and `GET` still returns the owner afterward with `deleted: true`.\n\n3. **`rest/validation/DuplicateOwnerValidator.java`** \u2014 The blocking household-duplicate check now filters out `deleted` owners, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match has been soft-deleted.\n\n4. **`rest/validation/PossibleDuplicateDetector.java`** \u2014 The soft possible-duplicate/identity match likewise ignores deleted owners, keeping the two create-time checks consistent.\n\n5. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`, mapped automatically by MapStruct).\n\n6. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column to the `owners` table (`DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL` for HSQLDB grammar).\n\nThe repository's `delete(Owner)` remains as a general capability but is no longer on the owner-deletion path \u2014 the soft-delete logic lives in one place (the service), and the `deleted` state transition lives on the entity.\n\n### Tests\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` \u2705\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` \u2705\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2/2 passing.",
